  "live_records": {
    "q-90531": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90531",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{4}{3{x}^{3}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =2-{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
